; ted-donew-allocnull-ignored (#356): donew never reports a failed
; allocation: allocnull failing is ignored, firstitem, enditem and
; thisitem keep pointing at the freed lines of the old text.  TED alone
; under inject (alerts answered): a text of one line "abc", menu NEW
; (unchanged text: no requester); the 6th AllocMem of 10 bytes
; (MEMF_PUBLIC) of TED's process, NEW's allocnull, fails (the first
; five are made at the start, the fifth by the allocnull of the start's
; donew).  QUIT.
; Correct (the fix of the issue: outmem): the alert "Not enough memory
; for operation!"; the original goes on with the freed lines.
; @file bo.bas "abc\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts allocfail=10-10/f=1/1+5 blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
timeout 20
wait screen
menu 0 0
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
